   "text": "http : / / mybroadband . co . za / news / telecoms / 31714 - seacom - downtime - explained . html SEACOM <13 downtime> <4 explained> SEACOM <5 experienced> <6 downtime> this morning ; SEACOM <7 explained> that the <8 downtime> was most likely <2 caused> by a <9 problem> on SEA - ME - WE 4 August 16 , 2011 Numerous broadband users <10 complained> about international <52 connectivity> <16 problems> this morning , <3 caused> by <11 problems> on the SEACOM cable . SEACOM <12 confirmed> the <14 problems> on their Twitter account . \"We can <15 confirm> that SEACOM is currently <19 experiencing> <17 problems> on their network . We will <1 keep> you <20 updated> on <21 progress> , \" SEACOM <26 tweeted> at 09 : 30 this morning ( Tuesday 16 August 2011 ) . According to SEACOM's Suveer Ramdhani initial feedback points to a problem on the SEA - ME - WE 4 which caused downtime of around an hour on Tuesday . The downtime started at around 08 : 30 on Tuesday , and was resolved at approximately 09 : 40 . \"SEACOM's partner network <22 experienced> a terrestrial fibre <18 cut> between Alexandria and the Suez this morning 16th August from 06 : 31GMT . All links are back up as of 07 : 35GMT . Total <23 downtime> was 1hr 4 mins , \" SEACOM <25 said> in an official <24 statement> . MWEB CEO Rudi Jansen said that their business clients experienced no service interruptions because of the SEACOM downtime , and that their residential clients may have experienced some slow international connectivity . MWEB has automatic failover on SAT - 3 in the event of SEACOM outages to minimize the impact on their subscribers .",
